# `Queue` and `Deque`

## `Queue` — FIFO, prefer the signalling forms

```java
Queue<Task> q = new ArrayDeque<>();
q.offer(taskA);   // add at back  (add() throws)
q.peek();         // front, no remove → null if empty
q.poll();         // remove front → null if empty
```

`offer`/`poll`/`peek` signal · `add`/`remove`/`element` throw.

## `Deque` — both ends → also a stack

```java
Deque<Page> history = new ArrayDeque<>();
history.push(page);      // = addFirst
Page back = history.pop();   // = removeFirst — LIFO
```

## `ArrayDeque` — the one to remember

- Standard impl of **both** queue & stack — O(1) both ends
- **Avoid `Stack`** (legacy, synchronized) and `LinkedList` → use `ArrayDeque`
- Forbids `null` elements

## `PriorityQueue` — smallest first

```java
pq.offer(5); pq.offer(1); pq.poll();   // 1 — min, not oldest
```

Heap, O(log n): schedulers, top-k, Dijkstra.
